    <DataNode elementId="CPD-697" textLabel="brassinolide" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="IXVMHGVQKLDRKH-KNBKMWSGSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="100.0" centerY="870.92919921875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco">The C&lt;sub&gt;28&lt;/sub&gt; brassinosteroid |FRAME: CPD-697| (BL) is the most biologically active and together with its C&lt;sub&gt;28&lt;/sub&gt; congeners is distributed widely in the plant kingdom |CITS:[15012241]|. Brassinolide was the first isolated brassinosteroid, when pollen from |FRAME: TAX-3708| was shown to promote stem elongation and cell divisions, and the biologically active molecule was isolated |CITS: [Grove79]|.</Comment>
